{"id":"n-20261011-d300a5","category":"sports","display_title":"Eli Dasa Joins Maccabi Haifa","display_title_he":"אלי דסה מצטרף למכבי חיפה","short_summary":"Israeli national team captain Eli Dasa has ended his period without a club by signing a two-year contract with Maccabi Haifa, returning to the Israeli Premier League after seven years abroad.","english_level":"C1","words":461,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Ynet","domain":"ynet.co.il","url":"https://www.ynet.co.il/sport/israelisoccer/article/bkjdwpuogl","title":"חיזוק משמעותי לירוקים: אלי דסה סיכם לשנתיים במכבי חיפה","published_at":"2026-10-11T10:22:06.000Z"},{"name":"Walla","domain":"sports.walla.co.il","url":"https://sports.walla.co.il/item/3871720","title":"אלי דסה סיכם במכבי חיפה לשנתיים","published_at":"2026-10-11T13:16:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-11T10:22:06.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-11T13:11:44.556Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Israeli national team captain Eli Dasa has officially agreed to terms on a two-year contract with Maccabi Haifa, marking his dramatic return to the local Premier League after seven years playing abroad in the Netherlands and Russia. According to club announcements released on Sunday, the 33-year-old defender will wear green until the summer of 2028 and joins the squad immediately.","Dasa began the current season as an unattached free agent after parting ways with Dutch side NEC Nijmegen at the conclusion of the previous campaign. Although he initially hoped to secure another engagement in Europe, particularly within the Dutch league, he ultimately decided to conclude his search and accept the proposal from Haifa, bypassing potential moves and turning down links to Maccabi Tel Aviv and Hapoel Be'er Sheva. During his extensive career abroad, Dasa represented Vitesse Arnhem and Dynamo Moscow, following his initial departure from Maccabi Tel Aviv in September 2019. His impressive football resume includes early stints with Beitar Jerusalem, where he played between 2010 and 2015, alongside a domestic championship title won during the 2018/19 season with Maccabi Tel Aviv at Kiryat Shalom. Furthermore, he proudly serves as the captain of the Israeli national team, boasting a remarkable 81 international appearances to his name.","Despite starting the season without a club, national team coach Ran Ben Shimon previously summoned Dasa to the squad for the international window that concluded the previous week, a decision that drew considerable criticism. Across his career, Dasa has accumulated 213 appearances in the Israeli Premier League, alongside 93 matches in the Dutch league and 62 games in the Russian league.","The high-profile acquisition arrives at a very active period for Maccabi Haifa, who were busy preparing under coach Barak Bakar for an upcoming away league fixture against Hapoel Jerusalem at Teddy Stadium. The team has secured four victories out of their opening five matches of the campaign, including a narrow 3:2 triumph over Ironi Tiberias right before the international break. Meanwhile, current league leaders Maccabi Tel Aviv recently dropped two valuable points following a goalless draw against Bnei Sakhnin, narrowing the gap at the top.","Addressing the media during a press conference ahead of the match in the capital, Bakar noted that his squad possesses a nearly full roster, with the sole exception of Cedric Don, who sustained an injury. He emphasized that although the team is in a positive position, substantial improvements are still required. Bakar also openly addressed the disappointing situation regarding the visiting supporters, who decided to boycott the game, stating that football simply is not the same without fans in the stands, though he expressed understanding for their stance. Regarding the upcoming opposition, the coach insisted that history holds no relevance, framing it as a brand-new season filled with new players and warning that they face a dangerous, high-scoring opponent."],"facts":[{"fact":"Eli Dasa agreed to a two-year contract with Maccabi Haifa and will join immediately until the summer of 2028.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Dasa, 33, started the season without a club after leaving Dutch side NEC Nijmegen at the end of last season.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"He returns to the Israeli Premier League after seven years abroad playing in the Netherlands and Russia.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Before moving abroad in September 2019, Dasa played for Beitar Jerusalem and Maccabi Tel Aviv, winning a championship with Maccabi in 2018/19.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Abroad, he played for Vitesse Arnhem, Dynamo Moscow, and NEC Nijmegen.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Dasa serves as the captain of the Israeli national team and has accumulated 81 appearances.","sources":[2]},{"fact":"Maccabi Haifa's coach Barak Bakar prepares his squad for an upcoming away match against Hapoel Jerusalem at Teddy Stadium.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Maccabi Haifa has won four of its first five league matches this season, while league leaders Maccabi Tel Aviv drew 0-0 against Bnei Sakhnin.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Israeli","lemma":"Israeli","pos":"adjective","he":"ישראלי","name":null},{"text":"national","lemma":"national","pos":"adjective","he":"לאומי","name":null},{"text":"team","lemma":"team","pos":"noun","he":"נבחרת","name":null},{"text":"captain","lemma":"captain","pos":"noun","he":"קפטן","name":null},{"text":"Eli Dasa","lemma":"Eli Dasa","pos":"proper noun","he":"אלי דסה","name":"Eli Dasa"},{"text":"has","lemma":"have","pos":"verb","he":"יש","name":null},{"text":"officially","lemma":"officially","pos":"adverb","he":"רשמית","name":null},{"text":"agreed","lemma":"agree","pos":"verb","he":"הסכים","name":null},{"text":"to","lemma":"to","pos":"preposition","he":"ל-","name":null},{"text":"terms","lemma":"term","pos":"noun","he":"תנאים","name":null},{"text":"on","lemma":"on","pos